okens":34796.0,"llm_calls":1,"output_tokens":1291.0,"requests":3}}}},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State and verify how a vote-reset re-enters the reconciler's events-log ?t1= window (e.g. the reset POST emits a fresh comment-added event carrying patchSet.revision/ref), or add a reconciler input that does not depend on the events-log window, so restart recovery holds even when the change's original patchset-created event has aged past the cursor.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","drop_reason":null,"evidence":["reconcile.py:238 `candidates = _candidate_events(events, cfg.project)` — candidates come only from the events-log window, not from 'changes with a missing vote'","reconcile.py:14-18 the ?t1= window is a 'SERVER-SIDE INCLUSIVE LOWER BOUND … anything the cursor moves past is gone from every future window, permanently'","reconcile._candidate_events requires `patchSet.get('revision')` and `patchSet.get('ref')` (reconcile.py:178) and status NEW","Plan Context: the fix targets exactly the case where 'the receiver exits before that event is processed'"],"finding":"The reconciler only re-drives changes present in the events-log ?t1= low-water-mark window (reconcile._candidate_events over gc.list_events(cursor)); resetting the LLM-Review vote to 0 does not by itself create a reconciler candidate. Restart recovery of a rerun/recheck target therefore silently depends on the reset POST emitting a fresh events-log event that still carries patchSet.revision/ref, so an accepted rerun on a change whose patchset-created event has already aged past the cursor is never recovered.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fd4ff594a90fda40b","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan step 3 / step 6; reconcile.py reconcile_once + _candidate_events","norm_id":"n52ec50f86e1b45ca","priority":0.8,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","scenarios":["Operator /rerun (or accepted recheck-review) on a change whose patchset-created event predates the reconciler cursor; receiver restarts with a fresh queue before the forced event is drained; the change is not in the current events-log window so the reconciler never re-drives it despite the reset vote"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","drop_reason":null,"evidence":["4 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify whether the Gerrit reset must clear ALL accounts' non-zero LLM-Review votes on the revision (not just the bot's), or scope the 'review is owed' predicate to the bot's own vote, so reset-to-0 and the reconciler's vote-existence check are actually consistent.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","drop_reason":null,"evidence":["gerrit_client.py:206-222 iterates `entry.get('all')` (per-account) and returns True if `int(vote.get('value')) != 0` for ANY account","has_llm_review_vote docstring: 'any non-zero value means the patchset has already been voted (by the bot or an admin)'","Plan AC: 'a missing nonzero LLM-Review vote on the exact revision means review is owed'"],"finding":"The plan treats 'reset LLM-Review to 0' and 'no nonzero Gerrit vote' as equivalent, but has_llm_review_vote returns True on ANY non-zero per-account vote in labels.LLM-Review.all. A single POST under the bot account zeros only the bot's own vote; a non-zero vote cast by an admin account on the same revision would still make has_llm_review_vote True, so reconcile would still skip and the recovery would not fire.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ff644004a76e7c80d","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan steps 1-2 (Gerrit reset op) + step 5 (normal already-voted path); gerrit_client.has_llm_review_vote","norm_id":"n513503614f9fe62f","priority":0.2567,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":["A revision carries the bot's stuck -1 plus an admin's non-zero LLM-Review vote; /rerun resets the bot vote to 0 but the admin vote remains non-zero, so has_llm_review_vote stays True and the reconciler never re-drives the recovered revision"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7778,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify reconciler behavior when the Gerrit vote query fails/times out (fail-closed: do NOT clear the local voted row and retry next cycle) so a transient Gerrit error is never misread as 'no vote'.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5b","T5d","T5e","T9"],"criteria":["T5b","E6"],"decision":"dropped","drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Step 3: 'Reconcile Gerrit state before trusting local dedup. When the exact revision has no nonzero Gerrit vote, clear its stale local voted row and run the ordinary review path.'","ABSENCE: no stated handling for a failed/errored Gerrit query during reconciliation — a transient error could be misread as 'no vote' and trigger clearing the local row + re-review, or could abort reconciliation and lose recovery."],"finding":"The plan specifies atomicity for the acceptance path (do not ack if Gerrit reset fails) but does not specify the reconciler's behavior when the Gerrit vote query itself fails or times out during reconciliation.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fd0c226e2b84939ed","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan step 3 / reconciliation acceptance criteria","norm_id":"n0de9f392adf1272c","priority":0.066,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","scenari